	<trans-unit id="Reader Apps allow users to access previously purchased content. The only difference between Reader Apps and apps where the Reader App mode is not enabled is that users' registration is not available within the Reader App, so it needs be done from the desktop platform." extradata="mobile">
		<source><![CDATA[Reader apps allow users to access previously purchased content. The only difference between reader apps and apps where the reader app mode is not enabled is that users' registration is not available within the reader app, so it needs be done from the desktop platform.]]></source>
		<target><![CDATA[As aplicacións lectoras permiten aos usuarios acceder ao contido comprado anteriormente. A única diferenza entre as aplicacións de lector e as aplicacións nas que o modo de aplicación de lector non está activado é que o rexistro dos usuarios non está dispoñible dentro da aplicación de lector, polo que debe facerse desde a plataforma de escritorio.]]></target>
	</trans-unit>
	<trans-unit id="Reader Apps will let users access previously-purchased content, but will disable in-app user registration. New users can still register on desktop. This is due to an Apple policy, which you can read more about {linkOpeningTag}here.{linkClosingTag}" extradata="mobile">
		<source><![CDATA[Reader apps will let users access previously-purchased content, but will disable in-app user registration. New users can still register on desktop. This is due to an Apple policy, which you can read more about {linkOpeningTag}here.{linkClosingTag}]]></source>
		<target><![CDATA[As aplicacións de lectores permitirán aos usuarios acceder ao contido comprado anteriormente, pero desactivarán o rexistro de usuarios na aplicación. Os novos usuarios aínda poden rexistrarse no escritorio. Isto débese a unha política de Apple, sobre a que podes ler máis información {linkOpeningTag}aquí.{linkClosingTag}]]></target>
	</trans-unit>
